1. **An radio-frequency (RF) ranging system, comprising:**  

   a first interrogator configured to transmit a first RF interrogation signal and receive an RF response signal;  

   a second interrogator spaced apart from the first interrogator and configured to transmit a second RF interrogation signal and receive the RF response signal;  

   synchronization circuitry configured to synchronize the first and second interrogators to a common timing reference;  

   a target device comprising a mixing circuit configured to receive the first and second RF interrogation signals, mix the first and second RF interrogation signals to generate a mixed RF signal having at least one frequency component determined by respective frequencies of the first and second RF interrogation signals, and transmit the RF response signal based on the mixed RF signal; and  

   processing circuitry configured to determine a first distance between the first interrogator and the target device from a timing or phase relationship between the first RF interrogation signal and the RF response signal received by the first interrogator, and to determine a second distance between the second interrogator and the target device from a timing or phase relationship between the second RF interrogation signal and the RF response signal received by the second interrogator.
